336 - There Is a Fountain
 / 
Key: Bb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 336
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[Bb]There is [Eb]a[Bb]fountain [Eb]filled with [Bb]blood
[Bb]Drawn from [Eb]Emman[Bb]uel's [F]veins;
[Bb]And sin[Eb]ners [Bb]plunged be[Eb]neath that [Bb]flood
[Bb]Los[F7]e[Bb]all their [F7]guilty [Bb]sta[Eb]ins[Bb].
[F7]Lose [Bb]all their [F7]guilt[Bb]y[Eb]stains,
[Eb]Lose [Bb]all their [Eb]guilt[Bb]y[F]stains;
[Bb]And sin[Eb]ners [Bb]plunged be[Eb]neath that [Bb]flood
[F7]Lose[Bb]all their [F7]guilty [Bb]sta[Eb]ins[Bb].

Verse 2:
[Bb]The dying [Eb]thief rejoiced [Bb]to see [Eb]that fountain [Bb]in his day;
[Bb]And there may [Eb]I, though vile [Bb]as he, wash [F]all my sins away.
[Bb]Wash all [Eb]my sins [Bb]away, wash [Eb]all my [Bb]sins away;
[Bb]And [F7]there may [Bb]I, though [F7]vile as [Bb]he, wash [Eb]all my [Bb]sins away.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Thou dying [Eb]Lamb, Thy [Bb]precious blood [Eb]shall never [Bb]lose its power
[Bb]Till all the [Eb]ransomed church of [Bb]God are saved, [F]to sin no more.
[Bb]Are saved, [Eb]to sin [Bb]no more, are [Eb]saved, to [Bb]sin no more;
[Bb]Till [F7]all the [Bb]ransomed church [F7]of God [Bb]are saved, [Eb]to sin [Bb]no more.

Verse 4:
[Bb]E'er since, [Eb]by faith, [Bb]I saw the [Eb]stream Thy [Bb]flowing wounds supply,
[Bb]Redeeming love has [Eb]been my theme, [Bb]and shall be [F]till I die.
[Bb]And shall [Eb]be till [Bb]I die, and [Eb]shall be [Bb]till I die;
[Bb]Redeeming [F7]love has [Bb]been my [F7]theme, [Bb]and shall [Eb]be till [Bb]I die.

Verse 5:
[Bb]Lord, I [Eb]believe Thou [Bb]hast prepared, [Eb]unworthy though [Bb]I be,
[Bb]For me [Eb]a blood-bought free [Bb]reward, a golden [F]harp for me!
[Bb]A golden [Eb]harp for [Bb]me! A [Eb]golden harp [Bb]for me!
[Bb]For [F7]me a [Bb]blood-bought [F7]free reward, [Bb]a [Eb]golden harp [Bb]for me!

Verse 6:
[Bb]There in [Eb]a nobler, [Bb]sweeter song, I'll [Eb]sing Thy [Bb]power to save,
[Bb]When this poor [Eb]lisping, stammering tongue [Bb]is ransomed from [F]the the grave.
[Bb]Is ransomed [Eb]from the [Bb]grave, is [Eb]ransomed from [Bb]the grace;
[Bb]When [F7]this poor [Bb]lisping, stammering [F7]tongue [Bb]is ransomed [Eb]from the [Bb]the grave.
